module electroporationAssay
module cytokineDetection

manifest sampleMixture
manifest highConductivityBuffer
manifest cultureMedia

instructions:

// STEP 1: Sample droplet
// Per the paper, cells + target payload are co-resuspended TOGETHER in a
// single tube before being loaded into the middle reservoir, so this is
// modeled as one dispense of a pre-mixed sample, not three separate
// on-chip dispense+mix operations (which would wrongly inflate the
// droplet to 3 units before merging with the flanks).
// Cell count: 20000 - 40000 cells per reaction (triDrop optimum)
// sampleMixture = mammalianCells + lowConductivityBuffer + plasmidPayload,
// pre-combined off-chip at >= 2x10^7 cells/mL

sampleDroplet = dispense 1 units of sampleMixture

// STEP 2: triDrop three-droplet fusion
// Two flanking high-conductivity droplets isolate cells from metal electrodes,
// focusing a homogenous electric field (~0.55 kV/cm) across the sample droplet.
// 1 unit (sample) + 1 unit + 1 unit (flanks) = 3 units total, matching the
// paper's ~3 microliter total triDrop volume.

flank1 = dispense 1 units of highConductivityBuffer
flank2 = dispense 1 units of highConductivityBuffer

triDropStage1  = mix flank1 with sampleDroplet for 3s
triDropMerged  = mix triDropStage1 with flank2 for 3s

// STEP 3: Electroporation pulse
// NOTE: BioScript has no native voltage-pulse primitive. The 3 x 200 VDC,
// 10 ms pulses are approximated here with three discrete "heat" calls purely
// to mark timed energy-delivery events in the IR/DAG. This is a SYNTACTIC
// STAND-IN ONLY: 200C is not a real temperature for this step and must never
// be sent to a physical DMF actuator or a thermally-accurate simulator, since
// it would destroy the droplet rather than electroporate it.

heat triDropMerged at 200c for 10ms
heat triDropMerged at 200c for 10ms
heat triDropMerged at 200c for 10ms

// STEP 4: Off-chip transfer and recovery
// Per the paper, electroporated cells are pipetted off-chip directly into a
// well plate PRE-LOADED WITH WARMED CULTURE MEDIA, not back into
// electroporation buffer (prolonged EP-buffer exposure is explicitly noted
// as detrimental to viability, so reusing electroporation buffer here would
// contradict the protocol's own stated rationale).
// Max EP-buffer exposure time: 20 minutes.

cultureMediaDrop = dispense 1 units of cultureMedia
recoveredCells   = mix triDropMerged with cultureMediaDrop for 5s

// STEP 5: Post-electroporation incubation at 37C for >24h
// triDrop achieves greater than 90 percent viability at 24h post-EP

heat recoveredCells at 37c for 24h

// STEP 6: Detect transfection efficiency and viability via flow cytometry

transfectionSignal = detect electroporationAssay on recoveredCells for 30s
viabilitySignal    = detect cytokineDetection on recoveredCells for 30s

// STEP 7: recoveredCells is NOT disposed here - BioScript's "drain"/"dispose"
// primitives are equivalent (both consume the droplet permanently), so a
// conditional dispose on transfectionSignal would discard the sample either
// way. There is no "keep"/"output" primitive distinct from disposal, so the
// cells are simply left as the final output of the assay.

dispose transfectionSignal
dispose viabilitySignal
